@* FileUpload's Overview, written by hand after TextField's and the selection Overviews: one file
   posted (previewed in each mode), several files, required and disabled, checking on the server,
   interactive pages and its own words. Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A file upload is a drop zone where the user drops files or clicks to choose them. The zone is a real file input with a label that opens the picker, so it works on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor> with JavaScript off. The file posts with the form, and the page binds it by its <Code>Name</Code>. Set <Code>Multipart</Code> on the <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>, or only the file's name posts.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Types, size and posting</Heading>
<TextBlock>The zone can limit the file types it offers and the largest file it accepts, and it shows both under the prompt ("PNG or JPEG · up to 2 MB"). Set <Code>Accept</Code> to the types, and <Code>MaxFileSize</Code> to the largest size in bytes. On static pages, bind the file to an <Code>IFormFile</Code> property with <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm]</Code>, named like the field.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="file-upload-photo" />
<TextBlock>Both limits only guide the browser. The picker's "All files" choice gets past <Code>Accept</Code>, and with JavaScript off nothing checks the size. Check both on the server, as this example does by size and by the file's first bytes.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Several files</Heading>
<TextBlock>The zone can accept several files at once. Set <Code>Multiple</Code>, and on static pages bind the files to an <Code>IReadOnlyList&lt;IFormFile&gt;</Code> or an <Code>IFormFileCollection</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="file-upload-multiple" />
<List>
    <ListItem>Every chosen file posts under the same name.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>A file dropped on the zone, or chosen again, replaces the earlier choice rather than adding to it.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>The zone doesn't list the files, so show what arrived after the form post.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Required and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>A required zone stops the form from posting without a file. Set <Code>Required</Code> to turn it on. To turn the zone off, set <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="file-upload-states" />
<List>
    <ListItem><Code>Required</Code> is the browser's check, so a crafted form post can still leave the file out. Check that it arrived on the server too.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>A file can't be read-only, so a read-only <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor> disables the zone.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>A disabled zone posts nothing, so keep its file on the server rather than clearing it after the form post. See <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor>.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Checking on the server</Heading>
<TextBlock>Check every file's size and type where you save it. Set the server's request limits to match <Code>MaxFileSize</Code>: by default, Kestrel rejects a request over 30,000,000 bytes (about 28.6 MB) before your code runs.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="csharp" Title="Program.cs">@Limits</Code>
<List>
    <ListItem>The posted content type and file name come from the browser and can be anything. Don't use either to name the saved file or to decide how it's served.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Check the file's first bytes for its type, as the photo example does.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When the app runs behind IIS, IIS has its own request limit (about 28.6 MB by default).</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">On interactive pages</Heading>
<TextBlock>On interactive pages, the zone can hand you the files as soon as the user chooses them, without a form post. Set <Code>OnChange</Code>; it receives each file as an <Code>IBrowserFile</Code>. Read each file with <Code>OpenReadStream</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Interactive</Code>
<List>
    <ListItem><Code>OnChange</Code> leaves out files over <Code>MaxFileSize</Code>, and passes at most <Code>MaxFiles</Code> files (10 by default).</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Code>OpenReadStream</Code> throws for a file over 512,000 bytes unless you pass a larger limit, so pass <Code>MaxFileSize</Code>.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The zone's prompt, the line under it and its error messages can all be changed. To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>ChooseText</Code>, <Code>DragText</Code></td><td>The prompt</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>AcceptText</Code></td><td>The line under the prompt. Set it to empty for none.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>TooLargeText</Code>, <Code>WrongTypeText</Code></td><td>The messages for a file that's too large or of the wrong type</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Form Model="Model" FormName="profile" Multipart OnValidSubmit="Save">
            <FileUpload Name="Avatar" Label="Profile photo" Accept="image/png,image/jpeg"
                        MaxFileSize="2_000_000" />
            <Button Submit>Save</Button>
        </Form>

        @code {
            // The file binds by its Name; check its size and type in Save.
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "profile")]
            private IFormFile? Avatar { get; set; }
        }
        """;

    private const string Limits = """
        using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.Features;

        // Kestrel's limit for the whole request (30,000,000 bytes by default).
        builder.WebHost.ConfigureKestrel(kestrel =>
            kestrel.Limits.MaxRequestBodySize = 12_000_000);

        // The limit for a form's files (128 MB by default).
        builder.Services.Configure<FormOptions>(form =>
            form.MultipartBodyLengthLimit = 12_000_000);
        """;

    private const string Interactive = """
        <FileUpload Name="Avatar" Label="Profile photo" Accept="image/png,image/jpeg"
                    MaxFileSize="MaxSize" OnChange="UploadAsync" />

        @* PhotoStore is your own service. *@
        @inject PhotoStore Photos

        @code {
            private const long MaxSize = 2_000_000;

            private async Task UploadAsync(IReadOnlyList<IBrowserFile> files)
            {
                if (files is not [var file]) return;
                await using var stream = file.OpenReadStream(MaxSize);
                // Check the file's first bytes for its type before keeping it.
                await Photos.SaveAsync(stream);
            }
        }
        """;
}
